<item>
            <title>[ZEPPELIN-6247] Fix flag parsing bug in FileInterpreter</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-6247</link>
                <project id="12316221" key="ZEPPELIN">Zeppelin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Description:&lt;br/&gt;
&#160; This issue fixes a bug in the FileInterpreter class where the dash character &lt;img class=&quot;emoticon&quot; src=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/images/icons/emoticons/forbidden.png&quot; height=&quot;16&quot; width=&quot;16&quot; align=&quot;absmiddle&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; border=&quot;0&quot;/&gt; was incorrectly included as a flag when parsing command arguments.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160; Problem:&lt;br/&gt;
&#160; The current implementation of parseArg() method in FileInterpreter.java incorrectly includes the dash character as a flag. When parsing command arguments like &quot;&lt;del&gt;l&quot;, the method adds both &apos;&lt;/del&gt;&apos; and&lt;br/&gt;
&#160; &apos;l&apos; to the flags HashSet instead of just &apos;l&apos;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160; Current code (line 73):&lt;br/&gt;
&#160; for (int i = 0; i &amp;lt; arg.length(); i++) {&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160; This causes the dash character to be incorrectly stored as a flag.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160; Solution:&lt;br/&gt;
&#160; Start the loop from index 1 to skip the dash character:&lt;br/&gt;
&#160; for (int i = 1; i &amp;lt; arg.length(); i++) {&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160; Impact Analysis:&lt;br/&gt;
&#160; - Current behavior is not affected because the existing code (HDFSFileInterpreter) only checks for specific flag characters like &apos;l&apos; and &apos;h&apos;&lt;br/&gt;
&#160; - However, this is a correctness issue that could cause problems in future implementations&lt;br/&gt;
&#160; - The fix ensures that only actual flag characters are stored in the flags set&lt;/p&gt;</description>
